Lab #17 – Stored DOM XSS

Vulnerable Functionality:

Blog comment section

Goal:

Trigger alert() using a stored DOM XSS payload.

Analysis:

The application tries to sanitize user input using JavaScript replace() to encode angle brackets ( and >).
replace() only replaces the first occurrence when a string is used as the search value.
Because of this, only the first set of angle brackets is encoded.
Any later angle brackets remain unchanged and are rendered as HTML.

Payload:

HTML
<><img src=1 onerror=alert(1)>

Explanation:

The first <> gets encoded by the filter.
The <img> tag remains untouched.
Invalid image source (src=1) triggers the onerror event.
alert(1) executes, confirming Stored DOM XSS.

Result:

Successfully triggered JavaScript execution via a stored comment.
Lab solved ✅

